// Title: Binary Proxy Execution Via Dotnet-Trace.EXE
// Sigma ID: 9257c05b-4a4a-48e5-a670-b7b073cf401b
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Jimmy Bayne (@bohops)
// Date: 2024-01-02 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: execution, stealth, T1218
// Description: Detects commandline arguments for executing a child process via dotnet-trace.exe
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate usage of the utility in order to debug and trace a program.
// References:
//   - https://twitter.com/bohops/status/1740022869198037480
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_dotnet_trace_lolbin_execution.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\dotnet-trace.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "dotnet-trace.dll") and (ProcessCommandLine contains "-- " and ProcessCommandLine contains "collect")
